684→## Reading large ranges
685→
686→A single `getValues()` / `getFormulas()` / `getBackgrounds()` call is capped at
687→**24 blocks**, a block being 500 rows x 20 columns — roughly 12000 rows of one
688→column. Over the cap the call throws (it never silently truncates) and the error
689→tells you how to split it.
690→
691→Read in chunks and aggregate as you go, keeping the aggregate rather than the rows.
692→Do not shrink the chunk "to be safe": every read re-assembles the whole document
693→upstream, so smaller chunks multiply the cost instead of spreading it.
